Subject: [PATCH] fix(block-entities): use shulker facing from Bedrock data

Bedrock stores the placed shulker facing in its block entity. Apply that value to the Java block state so boxes placed on walls and ceilings render and open in the correct direction.

Retain tile facing in ChunkTracker state reads used by prediction correction
and forced refreshes. Those reads formerly restored baseline facing=down
after the tile-oriented state was sent. Resolve tile rewrites from the raw
runtime mapping to retain each new facing update without recursion.

The actual state getter test covers absent and null tile data, retained west
facing, and subsequent down-facing updates.
